„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÚTo what purpose is the multitude of your sacrifices unto me? saith the LORD: I am full of the burnt offerings of rams, and the fat of fed beasts; and I delight not in the blood of bullocks, or of lambs, or of he goats.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZWhen ye come to appear before me, who hath required this at your hand, to tread my courts?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´Bring no more vain oblations; incense is an abomination unto me; the new moons and sabbaths, the calling of assemblies, I cannot away with; it is iniquity, even the solemn meeting.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmYour new moons and your appointed feasts my soul hateth: they are a trouble unto me; I am weary to bear them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“And when ye spread forth your hands, I will hide mine eyes from you: yea, when ye make many prayers, I will not hear: your hands are full of blood.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcWash you, make you clean; put away the evil of your doings from before mine eyes; cease to do evil;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙblearn to do well; seek judgment, relieve the oppressed, judge the fatherless, plead for the widow.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­Come now, and let us reason together, saith the LORD: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAIf ye be willing and obedient, ye shall eat the good of the land:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjbut if ye refuse and rebel, ye shall be devoured with the sword: for the mouth of the LORD hath spoken it.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrHow is the faithful city become an harlot! it was full of judgment; righteousness lodged in it; but now murderers.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ6Thy silver is become dross, thy wine mixed with water:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾thy princes are rebellious, and companions of thieves: every one loveth gifts, and followeth after rewards: they judge not the fatherless, neither doth the cause of the widow come unto them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTherefore saith the Lord, the LORD of hosts, the mighty One of Israel, Ah, I will ease me of mine adversaries, and avenge me of mine enemies:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^and I will turn my hand upon thee, and purely purge away thy dross, and take away all thy tin:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥and I will restore thy judges as at the first, and thy counsellors as at the beginning: afterward thou shalt be called, The city of righteousness, the faithful city.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJZion shall be redeemed with judgment, and her converts with righteousness.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€And the destruction of the transgressors and of the sinners shall be together, and they that forsake the LORD shall be consumed.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|For they shall be ashamed of the oaks which ye have desired, and ye shall be confounded for the gardens that ye have chosen.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPFor ye shall be as an oak whose leaf fadeth, and as a garden that hath no water.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~And the strong shall be as tow, and the maker of it as a spark, and they shall both burn together, and none shall quench them.¦layout ªlast_verse